{"availability":"available","full":"OnlyTerp/turboquant","name":"turboquant","description":"First open-source implementation of Google TurboQuant (ICLR 2026) -- near-optimal KV cache compression for LLM inference. 5x compression with near-zero quality loss.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":84,"forks":12,"created":"2026-03-25T10:11:04Z","updated":"2026-05-25T15:11:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":["attention","compression","deep-learning","google-research","iclr","kv-cache","kv-cache-compression","llm","llm-inference","machine-learning","memory-optimization","pytorch","quantization","transformer","vector-quantization","vllm"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/OnlyTerp/turboquant-demo","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T21:35:54.195Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T21:35:54.195Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T21:35:54.195Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:27.089Z","stars":81,"forks":11},{"at":"2026-10-11T02:07:25.674Z","stars":82,"forks":11},{"at":"2026-10-16T21:35:54.195Z","stars":84,"forks":12}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A data-oblivious KV-cache compressor. Random rotation + scalar Lloyd-Max quantizer that shrinks the KV cache to 3–4× smaller than FP16, no calibration data required. Useful when GPU memory is the binding constraint on your serving rig.","The related PolarQuant paper uses recursive polar coordinates, but TurboQuant deliberately avoids this. Recursive polar transforms couple coordinates through sin/cos operations at each level, causing errors to compound through deep models (7 levels for d=128). TurboQuant's scalar approach quantizes each coordinate independently — zero coupling, zero compounding."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OnlyTerp/turboquant/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"48ba0b731c4826bc380dbb58af5dc6325801c99b30f4f546683edd669042bcee","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:27.182Z"},"overviewC